      "digest": "b9f728aa5c7e84e0",
      "alt": "Pipeline diagram. Monocular RGB enters M2H-MX on the GPU, producing depth and semantics. Those feed pose-aware temporal alignment and a CPU-side VIO that uses predicted depth, with IMU input. The result is a metric semantic mesh and a 3D scene graph with building, room, place, object, and mesh layers.",
      "caption": "One camera and one IMU in, a layered scene graph out. The two arrows returning from odometry into the perception block are the part that distinguishes this from a feed-forward pipeline: pose stabilises the next prediction rather than only consuming it.",
      "credit": "Mono-Hydra++"
    },
